-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Base44 entity tables
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Generated by scripts/generate-entity-tables.mjs from the reference entity
-- schemas in interplanetarysister/interplanetary-fund2. Do not edit by hand;
-- re-run the script. See docs/migration/base44-entity-tables.json for the
-- machine-readable form of what follows.
--
-- Why these tables are needed
--
-- The reference backend has 184 function entrypoints that read and write 76
-- distinct entities. Only 10 of those entities had a table in this repository,
-- so a function could not be ported without its storage. That storage gap, not
-- the handler code, is the critical path of the backend migration, and this
-- migration closes it.
--
-- Column types follow the declared schema: string to text, number to numeric,
-- boolean to boolean, integer to integer, and any object or array to jsonb,
-- because the reference stores free-form structured values there and narrowing
-- them would reject data the application already accepts. A declared enum becomes
-- a check constraint, but only when every member is a usable string literal.
--
-- Every table also carries the Base44 implicit columns. They are not declared as
-- properties, but every record has them and the backend reads them: 75 functions
-- reference created_by_id and 53 reference created_date. created_at and updated_at
-- are also emitted here, because 16 and 12 entities declare them as properties and
-- the declared versions are skipped to avoid colliding with the implicit pair.
--
-- Access
--
-- Every table is deny-by-default: RLS is enabled and no privilege is granted to
-- anon or authenticated, and no policy is created. Nothing can read or write these
-- tables through a browser key until an access rule is written deliberately. The
-- ported handlers are expected to use a service-role client. Tables that do need
-- browser access, such as a member's own profile or follows, are granted in
-- 20261102_ifund_member_schema_completion.sql, which states the policy for each.
--
-- Applying this migration is additive. It creates tables and touches nothing that
-- already exists, so it is safe to apply before the reference data is imported.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- id is the original Base44 record identifier, which is text, not a uuid. The blog
-- tables already use this convention. Keeping the original id means imported rows
-- keep the identity that cross-references in the functions rely on.

